From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 18:32:53 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] um: wake the system through every descriptor of a shared
 interrupt

irq_set_irq_wake() reaches normal_irq_set_wake(), which marked the first
descriptor registered for the interrupt and stopped.  A system suspend
keeps only marked descriptors notifying, so input on any other
descriptor of the same interrupt could not end it.

A virtio_uml device shares one interrupt among its backend-request
channel, when it has one, and the call descriptor of every queue.  Only
the first of them was armed when wakeup was enabled in sysfs, so a
backend that wakes the guest by completing buffers on another queue left
it suspended.

Mark every descriptor registered for the interrupt, and clear every one
when wakeup is disabled again.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/um/kernel/irq.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/um/kernel/irq.c b/arch/um/kernel/irq.c
index 5f0f5df8be3588413636b27a81c957f55d2c18b2..5912f659c7d620bbeafdb6c26e476a6394e79681 100644
--- a/arch/um/kernel/irq.c
+++ b/arch/um/kernel/irq.c
@@ -652,6 +652,12 @@ void um_irqs_resume(void)
 	send_sigio_to_self();
 }
 
+/*
+ * An interrupt may be shared by several descriptors, as each queue and the
+ * backend channel of a vhost-user device share the device's, and input on
+ * any of them is input for the interrupt.  Every one of them wakes the
+ * suspended system, so every one carries the setting.
+ */
 static int normal_irq_set_wake(struct irq_data *d, unsigned int on)
 {
 	struct irq_entry *entry;
@@ -668,10 +674,8 @@ static int normal_irq_set_wake(struct irq_data *d, unsigned int on)
 			if (entry->reg[t].irq != d->irq)
 				continue;
 			entry->reg[t].wakeup = on;
-			goto unlock;
 		}
 	}
-unlock:
 	raw_spin_unlock_irqrestore(&irq_lock, flags);
 	return 0;
 }
